(Stage 1e2 - hash-table growth stress. 10,000 inserts with dynamic keys
 cross many doubling boundaries (8 -> 16 -> ... -> 16384 entries) and
 rehash each time. Length stays accurate and the first/last keys resolve
 to their inserted values. Acceptance: 10000, 0, 9999.)

a map called m is {}.
a number called i is 0.
while i is less than 10000, set m's "key{i}" to i, increment i.
a number called len is m's length.
a number called firstv is m's "key0".
a number called lastv is m's "key9999".
print len.
print firstv.
print lastv.